    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d335">

                <pb facs="0721" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg709"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to
                        Mr. Walter S. Robertson, at
                    Peiping</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-12">12 June 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>876. Chou En-lai requests that I instruct Executive Headquarters to order Team 32
                    to return to Hsuanhwatien and resume their team activities. Chou En-lai
                    intimates that American and Nationalist members of Team 32 are on an
                    unauthorized tour to the south towards Hankow. What is your knowledge of this
                    situation? Can you do something to get Team 32 reassembled and functioning
                    together, preferably at Hsuanhwatien?<anchor n="34" xml:id="d335-f1"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d335-f1" n="34" xml:id="d335-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 2900, June 12, Mr. Robertson informed General Marshall that
                    “there is no information available to us here now that indicates team 32 has
                    left its station at Hsuan Hua Tien nor that its team personnel is incomplete.”
                    Mr. Robertson added that the American member of the team had been asked to
                    submit a report.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
